  "scope_id": "SELECT-COUNT-20261101-001",
  "title": "Counted length is a measure on the knot's spaces",
  "subject": "Whether the number of witnesses along the routes of the knot's spaces forms a measure, and what it measures",
  "conclusion": "Across every nontrivial 2- or 3-edge cut of a knot's space each side has one count on its accepted channel values and the two counts multiply to the amplitude, so counted length (its logarithm) is additive over the decomposition: log 5 per Fano block plus the glue's tree-trinity logarithm, independent of the routes' relations and unchanged by transposition. It is a law-intrinsic measure on substrate routes, not a native extended distance.",
